# Opening Settings' Wi-Fi pane, so that something asks the radio to scan.
#
# iOS lists networks only while that pane is open: wifid asks apple80211 for a scan, the reference
# implementation's lx layer hands it to ath11k, the firmware answers. The pane is opened inside
# SpringBoard by libredwood-sb.dylib, which answers com.redwood.wifi by asking LaunchServices for
# "App-Prefs:root=WIFI" (src/inject_sb.c, open_wifi_settings).
#
# The wait is a `sleep` of its own -- a fresh process that sleeps once -- and then rwtouch only posts
# the notification. That split is the one that works: src/sleep_test.c (rc.jobs.sleep) showed six
# waits in one process coming back on the dot (3, 202, 1003, 5004, 2004, 2004 ms) and the seventh
# never returning, and a thread inside SpringBoard woke from one sleep and not its second. So no
# process here waits twice, and SpringBoard waits not at all.
sleep 20
/redwood/bin/rwtouch notify com.redwood.wifi
sleep 20
/redwood/bin/rwtouch notify com.redwood.wifi
